Interestingly, the w8-a8 configuration consistently surpasses w4-a16, highlighting the importance of weight quantization. Overall, reconstruction-based and hybrid quantization methods outperform scale-based transformations under low-bit settings. These patterns are consistent across all Whisper and Moonshine variants, confirming that while $8$-bit precision is generally safe for deployment, lower-bit weight quantization requires careful algorithmic design and model capacity considerations. As a reference, the runtime cost of each quantization algorithm is available in Appendix \ref{appendix:runtime}.


