\subsubsection{Weight clipping}
\label{sub:clipping}
The technique of weight clipping is commonly used to constrain the range of weight values prior to quantization. By suppressing extreme outliers, it reduces quantization error. However, this process may also introduce clipping loss, potentially harming model accuracy. To investigate this trade-off, we use AWQ as a case study to evaluate the impact of weight clipping under four bit-width settings: w4-a8, w4-a16, w8-a8 and w8-a16 on both Whisper Tiny and Whisper Base models. Table \ref{tab:weigt_clipping} reports the resulting averaged WER across all seven evaluation datasets. 

